# These files' own content (SPDX identifiers, license names, and example
# license text used for detection/testing logic) is mistaken by scancode for
# an added license. Narrowing this list depends on the scancode-toolkit
# version bump (separate branch) -- 32.2.1's matcher is prone to exactly this
# kind of false positive; re-check each file below once that lands.
#
# - main.py, scanner/license_scancode.py: docstrings extensively name real
#   SPDX identifiers (BSD-3-Clause-Clear, MIT, GPL-2.0, LicenseRef-scancode-*)
#   to document the proprietary-mode rules; this is prose, not data that
#   moved anywhere in Step 3.
# - scanner/config.py: a project-name -> license-string mapping table; the
#   license identifiers are the file's entire content, not incidental data.
# - scanner/copyright_checker.py: holds the QUIC -> QTI copyright transition
#   strings and DEFAULT_INTERNAL_ENTITIES verbatim, which read as copyright
#   changes whenever this file itself changes.
# - .licenseignore (this file): explaining the exclusions above means naming
#   real SPDX identifiers as examples, which trips the same false positive
#   -- confirmed the hard way, when this comment block itself got flagged.
main.py
scanner/config.py
scanner/license_scancode.py
scanner/copyright_checker.py
.licenseignore

